-- title:
--   Base change of power-series quotients by ideals containing (X)^N
-- statement:
--   Let $\sigma$ be a finite type of variables, $R$ a commutative ring, $S$ a commutative $R$-algebra, and $\varphi : \iota \to R[[X_\sigma]]$ a family, indexed by an arbitrary type $\iota$, of formal power series in the variables $X_s$ ($s \in \sigma$) over $R$. Assume that the $N$-th power of the ideal generated by the range of $X : \sigma \to R[[X_\sigma]]$ is contained in the ideal generated by the range of $\varphi$, for some natural number $N$. Write $\varphi_i^S \in S[[X_\sigma]]$ for the image of $\varphi_i$ under the coefficientwise map induced by $R \to S$. The assertion is the existence of an isomorphism of $S$-algebras
--   $$e : S \otimes_R \bigl(R[[X_\sigma]] / (\varphi_i : i \in \iota)\bigr) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S[[X_\sigma]] / (\varphi_i^S : i \in \iota)$$
--   which, moreover, sends $s \otimes [q]$ to $s$ acting by the $S$-module structure on the class of the coefficientwise image of $q$ in $S[[X_\sigma]]$, for all $s \in S$ and all $q \in R[[X_\sigma]]$. In other words, the canonical base-change morphism is an isomorphism, and $e$ is specified on generators.
--
--   This is the statement that formation of the quotient of a finite-variable power-series ring by an ideal containing a power of the ideal generated by the variables commutes with arbitrary base change — a property that fails for power-series rings themselves. It is used in the study of multivariate formal group laws, for the computation of the rank of quotients by the range of a homomorphism and for an identification of quotients of tensor products of such algebras.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_algEquiv_tensorProduct_quotient_span_map_of_pow_span_X_le.lean

